examples.question_text:
Amira and Ben share $\$84$ in the ratio $2:5$.
(a) How many equal parts are there altogether?
(b) How much does each person receive?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\node[left] at (-0.2,1.5) {Amira};
\draw (0,1) rectangle (2,2);
\draw (1,1)--(1,2);
\node[left] at (-0.2,0) {Ben};
\draw (0,-0.5) rectangle (5,0.5);
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,-0.5)--(\x,0.5);}
\draw (5.4,2)--(5.7,2)--(5.7,-0.5)--(5.4,-0.5);
\node[right] at (5.8,0.75) {$\$84$ total};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
(a) Total number of parts:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}2+5\\&=7\text{ parts}\end{aligned}$

(b) Divide by $7$ to find one part, then multiply for each share.
$\begin{aligned}7\text{ parts}&=\$84\\1\text{ part}&=\$84\div7\\&=\$12\\2\text{ parts}&=2\times\$12\\&=\$24\\5\text{ parts}&=5\times\$12\\&=\$60\end{aligned}$

Amira receives $\$24$ and Ben receives $\$60$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=11mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\node[left] at (-0.2,1.5) {Amira};
\draw (0,1) rectangle (2,2);
\draw (1,1)--(1,2);
\foreach \x in {0.5,1.5} {\node at (\x,1.5) {$\$12$};}
\node[left] at (-0.2,0) {Ben};
\draw (0,-0.5) rectangle (5,0.5);
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,-0.5)--(\x,0.5);}
\foreach \x in {0.5,1.5,2.5,3.5,4.5} {\node at (\x,0) {$\$12$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Check: $\$24+\$60=\$84$.
